{
 "sheet": 1,
 "name": "LTC1864CMS8#PBF",
 "kind": "adc",
 "manufacturer": "Analog Devices (Linear Technology)",
 "title": "Micropower 16-bit 250ksps 1- and 2-channel serial ADCs in MSOP (LTC1864/LTC1865)",
 "source": {
  "revision": "18645fs, LT/TP 0502",
  "pages": 20
 },
 "summary": "The LTC1864 and LTC1865 are 16-bit successive-approximation ADCs with built-in sample-and-hold, running at up to 250ksps from one 5V supply through a 3-wire SPI/MICROWIRE-compatible port. The LTC1864 has one true differential input and a reference pin; the LTC1865 has a 2-channel multiplexer picked over SDI, with a reference pin in the 10-lead MSOP and the reference tied to VCC in SO-8. The converter powers down between conversions, drawing 850µA typical at full rate and about 2µA at 1ksps. A-grade parts guarantee 15-bit no-missing-codes and ±6LSB INL.",
