  {
   "id": "two-channel-simultaneous",
   "title": "Sample two channels simultaneously with a single input ADC",
   "page": 20,
   "description": "Two AC-coupled signals are biased up from a divided 4.096V reference and sent one to each LTC1864 input. Channel f1 (0V to 0.66V) passes a non-inverting stage with a gain of 3 (20k over 10k, 5pF across the 20k); channel f2 (0V to 2V) passes a unity-gain follower. Each output reaches the ADC through 100Ω with 100pF to ground. Because IN+ and IN– are sampled at the same instant, the digital result is the difference of the two signals taken at one moment. The 4.096V reference drives VREF, bypassed by 0.1µF and 1µF; VCC at 5V has the same pair.",
